        tilesU: UDIM tiles across. Default 1.
        tilesV: UDIM tiles up. Default 1.
        region: Pack into [uMin, vMin, uMax, vMax] of each tile instead of all of it.
        texelsPerUnit: Pack at this density (px/cm) instead of filling the tiles; overflow spills into further tiles. Default 0.0.
        effort: Search effort 0-3: island orders tried per scale (1, 3, 6, 12). Higher packs denser, slower. Default 1.
        timeLimit: Stop refining after this many seconds (0 never); results can then vary between runs. Default 0.0.
        workingResolution: Search raster cells across a tile; 0 uses the resolution up to 4096. Default 0.
    """

def uvUnwrapSymmetric(uvSet: str | None = None, axis: str | None = None, mode: str | None = None, method: str | None = None, mirrorSeams: bool | None = None, pack: bool | None = None) -> Any:
    """Symmetry-aware unwrap of the selected faces using the mesh's symmetry pairs: islands on one side are solved and mirrored onto their partners (flip lays the mirror image beside, stack shares the same uvs), islands across the plane come out exactly mirror symmetric. Seams are mirrored first so islands pair up. With radial symmetry, one wedge's faces are unwrapped and every other wedge's copies stack on them.

    Args:
        uvSet: UV set; the current one (uvSetCurrent) when not given.
        axis: x, y, z, or auto: the mesh's symmetry axis, else x. One of 'auto', 'x', 'y', 'z'. Default 'auto'.
        mode: flip or stack. One of 'flip', 'stack'. Default 'flip'.
        method: slim, conformal or bff. One of 'slim', 'conformal', 'bff'. Default 'slim'.
        mirrorSeams: Copy seams across the plane first. Default True.
        pack: Pack into 0-1 afterwards. Default False.
    """

